{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532949-is-there-a-homebrew-that-helps-people-playing-vtm-solo","id":1532949,"title":"Is there a Homebrew that helps people playing vtm solo?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-21T11:19:12-07:00","id":1532949,"title":"Is there a Homebrew that helps people playing vtm solo?","content":"i'm getting into solo play,i wanted to know if there's any homebre guides for solo playing vtm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T17:44:05-07:00","id":1533097,"title":"","content":"Solo as in one player 1 storyteller? or just solo?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T17:45:05-07:00","id":1533098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532949-is-there-a-homebrew-that-helps-people-playing-vtm-solo?p=1533097#post1533097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solo as in one player 1 storyteller? or just solo?</div> </div> </div> </div>just solo,the one I'm studying rn is Tourniquet at the stv","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T19:30:00-07:00","id":1533104,"title":"","content":"So basically it's writing a story, but use dice to decide the outcome of events? I never tried it myself, I'm not sure what I could offer. Good luck with it, I'll follow the tread to see others ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T00:51:54-07:00","id":1533107,"title":"","content":"I... don't think it is possilbe in a game where you need a ST and a player<br /> By default a TTRPG have a 2 people requirment as bare minimum. One ST one Player<br /> It could maybe work out like the Fighting Fantasy books, a series of single-player role-playing gamebooks created by Steve Jackson and Ian Livingstone in the eighties (man I loved those)?<br /> Each <i>Fighting Fantasy</i> gamebook requires the reader to create their character, randomly assigning scores to three statistics (skill, stamina, and luck). These, in conjunction with rolling six-sided dice, are used to resolve skill challenges and the combat sections. Some titles use additional statistics or conflict resolution mechanics; most also require the reader to keep an inventory of items.<br /> And decide where to go next: if you want to check out the room, go to page 42, if you want to sneak around page 57.<br /> So by using a WoD caractersheet and the d10 system, with the premade enemies... It could work?<br /> Just before it could work you have to desing your own story with multiple branches and stroylines (not unlike they had in Shadow the Hedgehog with the numerous lines)<br /> To be enjoyable - sorry, lack of better words - you have to have a split personality 'tho...<br /> ...or grab a ST to do all this for you and you basically use the notes and script as your &quot;Fighting Fantasy book&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 03-25-2024, 04:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T04:23:38-07:00","id":1533116,"title":"","content":"I'm not aware of material to help with solo play, but maybe I can share some things from my own experience. I have an on-and-off solo campaign I use to test out ideas.<br /> <br /> First, it is much easier to run an open-ended sandbox than any official campaigns. The latter are written with a fixed narrative string the ST is supposed to lead the players along, and it's tricky to completely separate ST-only knowledge from player knowledge. I've found that preset campaigns tend to cramp solo play because twists, reveals, secrets, and so on don't work as well. It would be different for choose-your-own-adventure type of scenarios like Shadeprowler mentioned, but the official campaigns are written for ST/Player pairs and often require the ST to familiarize themselves with the campaign outline before playing.<br /> <br /> Taking a campaign setting (like one of the City books) and then throwing your PC into it is much easier, as you can evolve it according to your actions. The ST portion reduces pretty much to the usual 'How would NPC X react to what just happened?' and then you develop events from there. Gameplay is mostly unfolding from the PC perspective and the narrative is created from the actions you take. As usual, it helps to create complications that keep the game running. This also leaves you free to throw in events and twists you think would be interesting, or you can use plot events from the campaigns. As I said, I use solo play to test out ideas, so for me this usually means I insert a hook like I would for players in a group game.<br /> <br /> Running more than a single PC gets complicated, so if you plan to solo play a group I recommend keeping the perspective to one at a time. The advantage of solo play is that you don't have to worry about boring the rest of the players while one PC is doing things on their own. You can also insert downtime for characters more liberally and have them do things in the background for much the same reason. This helps with keeping the narrative going while off-screen characters perform tasks that would be boring for a player otherwise.<br /> <br /> I keep a log of events and actions of the PCs and NPCs, and use them in group play to flesh out background events if I decide to take an idea from the solo campaign to my group campaign. It's very helpful for developing NPC backgrounds and characteristics, because you already have played them in advance. It's also useful to test combat encounters.<br /> <br /> With all that said, there will always be unexpected turns in group play that solo play can not emulate. After all, you know yourself pretty well and can't truly surprise yourself. Dice rolls help a bit, but the narrative will follow along your own expectations. Don't let that stand in your way though- if you can accept that solo and group play are different beasts, you can still get some fun moments that simply evolved from your actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T08:24:25-07:00","id":1533252,"title":"","content":"On storyteller vault there is a book for solo vampire play. I downloaded it but have not used it to give a good review. <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/product/427846\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/product/427846</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T08:29:39-07:00","id":1533254,"title":"","content":"thank you lots","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T20:08:17-07:00","id":1533294,"title":"","content":"\u0130 know there are some systems out there where the ST is replaced by tables and dice rolls to generate randomly what one encounters. This should be suitable for a playstyle where one doesn't play through a preconceived plot, but simply move forwards based on how the player's choices interact with a partly randomly generated setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}